 5. Preserve negative and inconclusive evidence.
 6. Do not claim a strategy delta worked until its expected effect is actually observed.
 7. When there is insufficient evidence, choose UNVERIFIED rather than forcing RETAIN or REVERT.
 8. Selection and closure records must be reconstructible from durable state alone: every frontier closure must carry the activation ID that produced it, and every focused-task selection record must enumerate every role-eligible OPEN task with one index-aligned priority label per task. A closure or selection record that cannot be reconstructed is a traceability defect to be recorded explicitly, not silently accepted (observed: activation 44585034006 / P-001 — the cross-sectional-momentum closure carried no activation ID and no `STATE.md` section, and `selection_basis` listed 5 of 6 eligible tasks with 7 priority labels for 5 tasks).
+9. Verification independence must hold at the specification level, not only the implementation level. A verifier that re-implements the same formula from the same prose can detect implementation drift but cannot detect a wrong specification. Before a verdict is admitted, require a signal-level sanity check tied to the written definition: the signal takes both signs on real data, matches a hand-computed case, and its documented parameter dependence is non-degenerate. Observed: activation 44585034006 / R-001 — three prior momentum verifiers reproduced a `momentum_signals` that averaged log prices and was therefore a constant long position; all reported MATCH because they shared the specification defect.

